  "text": {
    "paragraphs": [
      "It is night, and the lamp is on. The family is in the living room. Mom, Dad, Tom, and Lily play a game. It is Who Is It? Pip sits next to Lily. \"Say one thing,\" says Dad. \"We say who it is.\" \"I start,\" says Dad.",
      "\"It is a man,\" says Dad. \"He likes fishing.\" \"Grandpa!\" says Tom. Mom says, \"It is a woman.\" \"She has glasses and a red dress.\" \"Grandma!\" says Lily. Tom says, \"It is a boy.\" \"He is nine years old.\" \"That is you, Tom!\" says Mom. They smile.",
      "Lily says, \"It is a child.\" \"She is seven, and he is my brother.\" Dad smiles. \"Is it you, Lily?\" he asks. \"Yes!\" says Lily. \"Woof!\" says Pip. \"Pip is a dog,\" says Tom. \"He is part of the family!\" says Lily. Then Mom has a letter from Grandpa. \"Tom, come fishing with me!\" Tom is very happy."
    ],
    "summary": "The family plays a guessing game at night. Each person says one fact about a family member, and then Mom reads a letter from Grandpa.",
